            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/review/app/stop.go: Stop returns early with no block when the Asked store is missing or when continuing is true, and neither case calls git or the stores. stop_test.go asserts both: TestStopRefusesToRunWithoutAStoreOfItsQuestions and TestStopDoesNotBlockWhileAStopHookIsContinuing.",
              "engine/review/app/stop.go: once() calls Has before Add, so a block is only returned after the question is recorded. A failure of Has or Add returns an error with no block, which avoids repeated blocking at later stops. TestStopDoesNotBlockWhatItCannotTellOrRemember covers the git, Has and Add failures.",
              "engine/review/app/unreviewed.go: NoDefaultBranchError keeps the original message text and Unwrap returns ErrNoDefaultBranch, so existing errors.Is callers still work. Stop uses errors.As to branch on the typed error.",
              "Dedup keys follow the stated design: a per-commit-range key, built from the first 12 characters of the base and head, and a single session-wide key for the no-default-branch case. Tests cover the same session, another session and the next commit.",
              "Residual gap, not a defect: no test checks that the no-default question is asked once per session across different branches, or the Has/Add error path for that question. The shared once() code covers those paths, so the behavior is still proved at the unit level."
            ]
          }
        }
      }
